Anyway, I won't bore y'all with correcting myself, but I will bring
out a brand new(?) method of swindling money from a shopkeeper that I
discovered in midgame (which the ttyrec log reminded me of).

Here's the scenario: the general shop in Minetown has been cleaned
out, and the SK is bankrupt, but I needed more money. So I went to the
tool shop, but it doesn't buy gems. So what's the solution? Put the
gems in my BoH (which also contains all the rest of my loot) and sell
the BoH. The BoH itself only nets a small sum, but the CONTENTS put
the SK in great debt of me. So, summon in the pet to whisk the bag
back out, and now the SK owes me $3500+ zm. Then go in with a unihorn
(or some other expensive tool), and repeatedly sell, pick it back up,
and pay from my credit---I don't even need to use my pet for this
step!  And so I managed to liquidate the SK's debt until he was
bankrupt, at which I just left him feeling really guilty. :-P


